1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,840
Good evening, welcome to the first and only debate in the Race for Governor of New York.

2
00:00:05,840 --> 00:00:10,760
I'm Errol Lewis, political anchor at New York One, coming to you live from our studios

3
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:11,760
here in Manhattan.

4
00:00:11,760 --> 00:00:14,640
And I'm Spectrum News political anchor, Susan R. Better.

5
00:00:14,640 --> 00:00:18,960
Tonight's broadcast can be seen on all of our stations across New York, and we are also

6
00:00:18,960 --> 00:00:23,360
streaming live on the Spectrum News app and on our YouTube channel.

7
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:29,320
Election Day is three weeks from tonight, and early voting kicks off on Saturday, October

8
00:00:29,320 --> 00:00:30,480
24th.

9
00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:34,640
New Yorkers will be casting their ballots in key congressional, legislative, and statewide

10
00:00:34,640 --> 00:00:38,800
races, including the one that we're focused on tonight, Governor of New York.

11
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:44,080
So tonight's debate is hosted under the auspices of New York State's public campaign finance

12
00:00:44,080 --> 00:00:45,080
board.

13
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:50,360
It's also being broadcast in Spanish by our colleagues at Spectrum Noticias.

14
00:00:50,360 --> 00:00:54,720
Over the course of the next hour, you'll hear from both candidates, Kathy Hochold is

15
00:00:54,720 --> 00:00:59,240
the incumbent, a Democrat, who has held the job since 2021.

16
00:00:59,240 --> 00:01:03,480
Our Republican challenger is Bruce Blakeman, who has served as National County Executive

17
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:05,640
since 2022.

18
00:01:05,640 --> 00:01:09,560
The rules you see on your screen have been agreed to by both candidates.

19
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:13,080
They will each have 60 seconds for an opening statement.

20
00:01:13,080 --> 00:01:17,800
Answers to our questions will generally be limited to 60 seconds with 30 seconds to answer

21
00:01:17,800 --> 00:01:21,360
rebuttals or follow-ups at our discretion.

22
00:01:21,360 --> 00:01:25,320
And there will be both a cross-examination round where the candidates get to ask one

23
00:01:25,320 --> 00:01:30,200
question to their opponent and a lightning round where their answers should be yes or

24
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:31,920
no or very short.

25
00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:34,480
We begin now with one minute opening statements.

26
00:01:34,480 --> 00:01:38,760
The order was determined by a random drawing earlier today on live television.

27
00:01:38,760 --> 00:01:40,480
We'll start with you, Mr. Blakeman.

28
00:01:40,480 --> 00:01:41,480
Good evening.

29
00:01:41,480 --> 00:01:43,000
Good evening, Governor.

30
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:46,720
And thank you to everybody out there that's watching this debate.

31
00:01:46,720 --> 00:01:51,680
It gives me an opportunity to speak directly to you and your families about issues that

32
00:01:51,680 --> 00:01:55,800
are important here in New York State that affect you each and every day.

33
00:01:55,800 --> 00:02:02,120
As I travel across the state, and it's a beautiful state, everywhere I go, people are telling

34
00:02:02,120 --> 00:02:07,000
me how they're struggling, struggling to pay their bills, and they're worried about

35
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:09,200
safety in their communities.

36
00:02:09,200 --> 00:02:13,960
Under Governor Holko, we are the highest tax state in America.

37
00:02:13,960 --> 00:02:18,880
Our utility bills are 70 percent higher than the national average, and because of policies

38
00:02:18,920 --> 00:02:23,880
like cashless bail, people feel unsafe in their own communities.

39
00:02:23,880 --> 00:02:30,160
As Governor, I will cut taxes, I will cut your utility bills in half, and I will create

40
00:02:30,160 --> 00:02:35,800
safer communities just like I did in my own county in Nassau County.

41
00:02:35,800 --> 00:02:42,720
And let me say this, Kathy Holko has spent $8 billion of your money on illegal migrants

42
00:02:42,720 --> 00:02:46,720
for free food, free housing, free transportation, and a free cell phone.

43
00:02:46,720 --> 00:02:50,680
That's your money that she spent on people who aren't New Yorkers.

44
00:02:50,680 --> 00:02:54,120
I believe she's got her priorities upside down.

45
00:02:54,120 --> 00:02:57,640
So I'm going to ask you to vote for change.

46
00:02:57,640 --> 00:02:59,600
What have you got to lose?

47
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:03,360
And vote for a better New York, and vote for Blakeman for Governor.

48
00:03:03,360 --> 00:03:04,360
Thank you.

49
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:05,360
Next is Ms. Holko.

50
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:06,360
Good evening.

51
00:03:06,360 --> 00:03:08,720
Well, thank you for hosting us this evening and counting executive.

52
00:03:08,720 --> 00:03:10,720
Good to see you this evening.

53
00:03:10,720 --> 00:03:15,480
My parents started married life in a trailer park near the Bethlehem Steel Plant.

54
00:03:15,480 --> 00:03:21,480
I used to work long hours after school every day to raise money for college at a pizzeria.

55
00:03:21,480 --> 00:03:24,920
You know, I never forgot where I came from and the struggles.

56
00:03:24,920 --> 00:03:31,880
And that's why, as Governor, I have been laser focused on affordability and your family safety.

57
00:03:31,880 --> 00:03:37,440
And that's why we've delivered the largest middle-class rate cut in 70 years.

58
00:03:37,440 --> 00:03:43,360
That's why we've delivered over $10 billion in energy rebates and inflation rebates and

59
00:03:43,840 --> 00:03:45,600
rebates to how people pay their bills.

60
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:53,080
But also this, New York State now has the lowest crime rates it's had in modern history.

61
00:03:53,080 --> 00:03:55,880
Now, we're not done yet.

62
00:03:55,880 --> 00:04:03,480
And you're going to hear a lot of, well, a lot of different opinions here this evening.

63
00:04:03,480 --> 00:04:05,480
And I want you to judge it this way.

64
00:04:05,480 --> 00:04:07,920
My opponent has said this.

65
00:04:07,920 --> 00:04:13,920
He says that he's going to bring Trump-style leadership to Albany.

66
00:04:13,920 --> 00:04:16,080
He says he's going to cut Medicaid in half.

67
00:04:16,080 --> 00:04:18,520
You heard him say that.

68
00:04:18,520 --> 00:04:21,600
And he's going to let ICE run rampant in our streets.

69
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:24,360
So this is your choice, New Yorkers.

70
00:04:24,360 --> 00:04:26,280
I'm not letting this happen.

71
00:04:26,280 --> 00:04:31,480
Working together with you, we will not, because your family is my fight.

72
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:33,840
Okay, thank you, candidates.

73
00:04:33,840 --> 00:04:37,840
We're going to begin tonight by discussing an incident that is reigniting a national

74
00:04:37,840 --> 00:04:38,840
debate.

75
00:04:38,840 --> 00:04:42,960
An ICE agent last Thursday shot a Dominican immigrant in the Upper Manhattan neighborhood

76
00:04:42,960 --> 00:04:46,520
of Marble Hill while his five-year-old son was in the backseat of the car.

77
00:04:46,520 --> 00:04:50,680
This took place on a busy street at a time many New Yorkers were making their way home

78
00:04:50,680 --> 00:04:52,680
from work or school.

79
00:04:52,680 --> 00:04:55,840
Federal government says the man drove towards agents before they shot him.

80
00:04:55,840 --> 00:04:58,240
I'm going to start with you, Mr. Blakeman.

81
00:04:58,240 --> 00:05:03,280
Multiple reports suggest that ICE has cut its training time, lowered its hiring standards

82
00:05:03,280 --> 00:05:08,040
and deployed masked agents in cities whose leaders don't want them there, in this case,

83
00:05:08,040 --> 00:05:11,320
with long guns in a crowded urban environment.

84
00:05:11,320 --> 00:05:14,400
And I guess the question is, are you comfortable with that?

85
00:05:14,400 --> 00:05:20,120
Kathy Hochle appealed to ICE to let this criminal out.

86
00:05:20,120 --> 00:05:24,760
The question that New Yorkers have to ask is, what was this guy doing in New York in the

87
00:05:24,760 --> 00:05:26,000
first place?

88
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:29,760
It's because Kathy Hochle has made us a sanctuary state.

89
00:05:29,760 --> 00:05:30,920
Think about it.

90
00:05:30,920 --> 00:05:36,520
This guy came into the country illegally, he's been convicted of a crime, he's got

91
00:05:36,520 --> 00:05:45,680
pending charges for dealing drugs poisoned to our children, and he's a gang banger.

92
00:05:45,680 --> 00:05:49,520
This is who Kathy Hochle is defending.

93
00:05:49,520 --> 00:05:54,560
I have a cooperative agreement with ICE until Kathy Hochle said we could no longer cooperate

94
00:05:54,560 --> 00:05:55,720
with ICE.

95
00:05:55,720 --> 00:06:00,920
We got over 2,000 illegal migrants out of my county with criminal records ranging from

96
00:06:00,920 --> 00:06:08,560
rape, attempted murder, robbery, burglary, drug dealing, carjacking, gang activity.

97
00:06:08,560 --> 00:06:13,520
And that's because we cooperated with ICE, and we didn't raid one school, one hospital,

98
00:06:13,520 --> 00:06:16,080
one day care center, or one church.

99
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:20,880
If you cooperate with federal law enforcement, it makes for a safer community, that's what

100
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:21,880
I did.

101
00:06:21,880 --> 00:06:24,400
Kathy Hochle has taken that ability away from us.

102
00:06:24,400 --> 00:06:26,320
That's why things like this happen.

103
00:06:26,320 --> 00:06:29,400
I had a question for you, Ms. Hochle, but I wanted to give you a chance to respond to

104
00:06:29,400 --> 00:06:30,400
you.

105
00:06:30,400 --> 00:06:31,400
No, thank you.

106
00:06:31,400 --> 00:06:34,400
I think in his non-answer, you refused to condemn what ICE did.

107
00:06:34,400 --> 00:06:40,800
So he basically says in the state of New York, he'd be fine if ICE agents shoot cars, shoot

108
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:48,120
into cars, shoot guns into vehicles, not knowing who's inside, and could have killed a five-year-old

109
00:06:48,120 --> 00:06:49,120
child.

110
00:06:49,120 --> 00:06:53,200
But that doesn't shock the conscience of everybody, and it should shock his conscience

111
00:06:53,200 --> 00:06:54,200
as well.

112
00:06:54,200 --> 00:06:56,080
That he says that's okay.

113
00:06:56,080 --> 00:06:57,080
That's how ICE is supposed to do it.

114
00:06:57,080 --> 00:07:02,200
I'll tell you what, I oversee over 500 policing agencies in the state of New York.

115
00:07:02,200 --> 00:07:04,120
Over half a million arrests every year.

116
00:07:04,120 --> 00:07:05,560
That's not how you conduct yourself.

117
00:07:05,560 --> 00:07:07,160
ICE is out of control.

118
00:07:07,160 --> 00:07:08,680
It's out of control in the ESO county.

119
00:07:08,680 --> 00:07:13,720
Kathy, if you ever would have happened, but for your sanctuary policy, you have invited

120
00:07:13,720 --> 00:07:18,920
criminals to come into our state and pray on our communities.

121
00:07:18,920 --> 00:07:24,240
And now you won't let local law enforcement cooperate with ICE in an orderly way, like

122
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:25,840
we did in my county.

123
00:07:25,840 --> 00:07:30,240
We didn't have any incidents in my county because we were allowed to cooperate with local law

124
00:07:30,240 --> 00:07:31,240
enforcement.

125
00:07:31,240 --> 00:07:32,840
But you took that tool away.

126
00:07:32,840 --> 00:07:38,160
The reason why that happened is because of you, Kathy Hochl, and your immigration policies,

127
00:07:38,160 --> 00:07:44,600
where you actually invite people into our state, give them free everything, and you don't

128
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:48,240
care whether they're criminals or not, that's a bad policy.

129
00:07:48,240 --> 00:07:52,720
I have a right to answer this one because this is so absurd.

130
00:07:52,720 --> 00:07:57,840
I have said, from the president on down, I said, New York is not as sanctuary for criminals.

131
00:07:57,840 --> 00:07:59,920
Not as sanctuary for criminals, full stop.

132
00:07:59,920 --> 00:08:05,800
But to say nothing happened in Nassau County, tell that to the man who, on camera, had his

133
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:10,600
head rammed into a brick wall by ICE agents who was knocked unconscious.

134
00:08:10,600 --> 00:08:15,520
Say that to the family of the man who died in York custody when he was in one of the Nassau

135
00:08:15,520 --> 00:08:16,800
counties jail.

136
00:08:16,800 --> 00:08:17,800
And nothing bad happens.

137
00:08:17,800 --> 00:08:24,200
We'll tell that to 11-year-old Norman, who sobbed in my arms when local police, Nassau

138
00:08:24,200 --> 00:08:29,360
police, took his father when he was just going to a home depot for God's sakes.

139
00:08:29,360 --> 00:08:32,880
And his father was sitting for months and months in the detention center.

140
00:08:32,880 --> 00:08:39,320
Kathy, how about the 230-year-old women who were murdered by an illegal migrant in my

141
00:08:39,320 --> 00:08:41,520
county?

142
00:08:41,520 --> 00:08:43,240
What do you say to their families?

143
00:08:43,240 --> 00:08:48,200
What do you say to all those people who have had their children hooked on drugs by illegal

144
00:08:48,200 --> 00:08:54,120
migrants, bringing fentanyl, cocaine, and heroin into our communities?

145
00:08:54,120 --> 00:08:59,920
We have an epidemic of crime from these illegal migrants, 16,000 detainers are out there for

146
00:08:59,920 --> 00:09:06,520
people who committed 52,000 crimes in our state, and you won't let local law enforcement cooperate

147
00:09:06,520 --> 00:09:10,200
with ICE to pick them up and get out of this state.

148
00:09:10,200 --> 00:09:13,720
This never would have happened, Kathy, if it wasn't for your policies.

149
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:17,960
You know his idea of law enforcement, because I have worked hard to drive down crime.

150
00:09:17,960 --> 00:09:22,200
I spent $4 billion of money to support our men and women in blue.

151
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:23,920
They know I have their backs.

152
00:09:23,920 --> 00:09:27,720
And I want to make sure that they're keeping our communities safe, not being deputized

153
00:09:27,720 --> 00:09:29,720
as ICE agents, which is what he did.

154
00:09:29,720 --> 00:09:36,440
And maybe that's why, maybe that's why Nassau County had a 10-year high in violent crimes

155
00:09:36,440 --> 00:09:40,680
under your watch, maybe because they're too distracted trying to be ICE agents.

156
00:09:40,680 --> 00:09:42,520
Well, I've talked to members of their police department.

157
00:09:42,520 --> 00:09:44,200
They just want to do their jobs.

158
00:09:44,200 --> 00:09:47,640
And when I changed the law, I got them back to local policing.

159
00:09:47,640 --> 00:09:50,520
So they can stop crimes, and they can respond to the police.

160
00:09:50,520 --> 00:09:55,000
I mean, you haven't heard U.S. News and World Report says I have the safest county in America.

161
00:09:55,560 --> 00:10:01,640
So I back one, and I back the laws of both our federal government and our state government.

162
00:10:01,640 --> 00:10:06,120
And I give our law enforcement professionals the tools they need to keep us safe.

163
00:10:06,600 --> 00:10:10,200
But you say you spent $4 billion on law enforcement.

164
00:10:10,200 --> 00:10:16,040
Well, you spent $8 billion on illegal migrants and gave them more benefits than New Yorkers get.

165
00:10:16,040 --> 00:10:17,880
How does that make any sense?

166
00:10:17,880 --> 00:10:22,760
I can't believe you just took credit for what the Democratic predecessor in your county did.

167
00:10:22,760 --> 00:10:25,480
Oh, she was the county executive in 2024?

168
00:10:25,480 --> 00:10:29,640
It was under Laura Curran that the crime started going down.

169
00:10:31,400 --> 00:10:32,760
They called Nassau down.

170
00:10:32,760 --> 00:10:33,800
Wasn't that during COVID?

171
00:10:33,800 --> 00:10:37,320
They called Nassau on one of the safest places in America

172
00:10:37,320 --> 00:10:39,080
before you became kind of executive system.

173
00:10:39,080 --> 00:10:42,760
Ms. Hochl, let me take credit for the sun rising in the morning and setting it nice.

174
00:10:42,760 --> 00:10:45,960
We're going to move on, but before we do, I wanted to ask you this, Ms. Hochl.

175
00:10:45,960 --> 00:10:52,440
Does New York's sanctuary policy amount to a cancellation at times of valid deportation orders

176
00:10:52,440 --> 00:10:55,560
provided an immigrant lays low and doesn't commit a violent crime?

177
00:10:55,560 --> 00:10:57,800
And are you comfortable with that reality?

178
00:10:57,800 --> 00:11:01,000
Even New York City has 170 crimes,

179
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:05,320
serious crimes where they will work with ICE agents to remove people.

180
00:11:05,320 --> 00:11:07,480
That is a fact all across the state of New York.

181
00:11:07,480 --> 00:11:11,320
We always work with law enforcement to remove people who are committing crimes.

182
00:11:11,320 --> 00:11:14,120
And the other thing is, when people commit a crime,

183
00:11:14,680 --> 00:11:16,600
I want them to go through our court system.

184
00:11:16,600 --> 00:11:19,080
I want victims to have their day in court.

185
00:11:19,080 --> 00:11:22,200
Then we kick them out of the country at the end of their prison term.

186
00:11:22,200 --> 00:11:26,280
That's how it's always operated, always work successfully,

187
00:11:26,280 --> 00:11:31,320
until you have rogue agents roaming the streets and counting executives like him supporting them.

188
00:11:32,520 --> 00:11:33,800
Okay, thank you, candidates.

189
00:11:33,800 --> 00:11:37,960
Thank you. We're going to move on now to voters' pocketbooks,

190
00:11:37,960 --> 00:11:39,560
and we're going to start with Kathy Hochl.

191
00:11:40,840 --> 00:11:45,000
Ms. Hochl, New Yorkers pay among the highest energy costs in the nation,

192
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:50,280
with experts saying that older plants are being shut down at a faster pace

193
00:11:50,280 --> 00:11:52,840
than the state can build new generation.

194
00:11:52,840 --> 00:11:58,040
And you've acknowledged that problem by sending out energy rebate checks to many New Yorkers,

195
00:11:58,040 --> 00:12:03,000
but the demand for energy continues and those prices continue to soar.

196
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:05,320
Well, these checks be going out annually.

197
00:12:05,320 --> 00:12:10,040
And beyond that, what are you doing in the short term to lower utility costs?

198
00:12:10,040 --> 00:12:11,240
You know, Susan, great question.

199
00:12:11,240 --> 00:12:13,800
I understand the pain that so many people are going through.

200
00:12:13,800 --> 00:12:16,280
Energy prices are high all over America.

201
00:12:16,280 --> 00:12:19,000
And the issue is, as you've put out so perfectly,

202
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:21,640
is that we don't have enough supply to meet the demand.

203
00:12:21,640 --> 00:12:23,800
So I have an all-the-above approach.

204
00:12:23,800 --> 00:12:27,320
I did do energy rebates just as a short-term solution,

205
00:12:27,320 --> 00:12:28,600
but I'm trying to build more.

206
00:12:28,600 --> 00:12:30,280
But you know what the real problem is?

207
00:12:30,280 --> 00:12:34,520
I've got Donald Trump standing the way of my energy projects

208
00:12:34,520 --> 00:12:38,840
literally shut down a project, picking 1,300 people off their jobs

209
00:12:38,840 --> 00:12:41,480
that would have powered half a million homes in Brooklyn.

210
00:12:41,480 --> 00:12:43,800
I also want to do part of my all-the-above.

211
00:12:43,800 --> 00:12:48,200
I'm trying to do nuclear, but the White House playing politics won't sign off by it.

212
00:12:48,200 --> 00:12:51,080
So we're doing the best we can, but don't overlook the fact.

213
00:12:51,640 --> 00:12:56,280
That is the war with Iran that is driving up gasoline costs and energy costs,

214
00:12:56,280 --> 00:12:58,200
almost double what they were in the past.

215
00:12:58,200 --> 00:13:01,000
Geeth Diesel is now double what it was.

216
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:04,440
That is a real cost of energy that people are dealing with,

217
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:06,120
and it was so unnecessary.

218
00:13:06,120 --> 00:13:09,480
And my opponent supports exactly what Donald Trump did with that war.

219
00:13:09,480 --> 00:13:11,400
Will you raise income taxes?

220
00:13:11,400 --> 00:13:13,240
Many of your progressive allies are saying...

221
00:13:13,240 --> 00:13:14,760
Can I respond to that first?

222
00:13:14,760 --> 00:13:17,480
Sure. I'd like to respond to the utility bill issue,

223
00:13:17,480 --> 00:13:20,680
because that's probably one of the most prevalent issues

224
00:13:20,680 --> 00:13:22,280
that we have here in New York.

225
00:13:22,280 --> 00:13:27,560
Uh, Kathy, Donald Trump didn't raise utility rates 48 times.

226
00:13:27,560 --> 00:13:28,680
You did.

227
00:13:28,680 --> 00:13:32,280
Donald Trump didn't increase our utility bills

228
00:13:32,280 --> 00:13:35,240
by 50% since you become governor.

229
00:13:35,640 --> 00:13:39,640
You gave $150 back to people in a rebate

230
00:13:39,640 --> 00:13:42,440
in an election year right before the election

231
00:13:42,440 --> 00:13:46,840
when you've raised the average bill $4,000 a year,

232
00:13:46,840 --> 00:13:49,960
and your own energy research department says

233
00:13:49,960 --> 00:13:54,520
your policies will raise another $4,000 in the next five years.

234
00:13:54,520 --> 00:13:56,120
